 { Before we begin to study pawn endgames, there is a concept that you need to be familiar with - opposition. There are many types of oppositions, but the one that you need to know for the time being is the direct opposition - that is, moving to the square two squares below the enemy King. By doing this, you take away ALL the advancing squares of your opponent’s King. With no other pieces interfering, once you get opposition, you should be able to maintain it indefinitely by following the Black King. } 1. { -KEY- } Ke4 Kd6 2. Kd4 Kc6 3. Kc4 Kd7 4. Kd5 Ke7 5. Ke5 Kf8 6. Kf6 Kg8 7. Kg6 Kh8 8. Kh6 
