 { Whenever you want to quickly calculate if a King can catch the enemy passed pawn in a basic king and pawn ending, we can use a method known as the pawn square. This method is far superior to conventional calculation methods because of its incredible efficiency. The concept is simple: Before the King moves, draw a diagonal line from the pawn to the last (promotion) rank. This will be the diagonal of a square known as the pawn square. If the King is able to enter the square, he can catch the pawn. Otherwise, the pawn queens unscathed. Here, the King can enter the box. Therefore, White catches the pawn and this is a draw. } 1. { -KEY- } Ke5 a4 2. Kd4 a3 3. Kc3 a2 4. Kb2 
