 { If the attacker has a bishop pawn or a central pawn, passive defence no longer works. Instead, we need to use the Philidor technique. The first step is to place our Rook on the third rank. This prevents the enemy King from advancing any further to threaten checkmate. } 1. { -KEY- } Rh3 { Passive defence does not work because Black can skewer our King and Rook from the other side. } ( 1. Rh1 Ra1 ) 
