 { If the pawn is on the sixth rank, the way to draw is by checking and pressuring the pawn from the side, where the a7 pocket will be ineffective. This is known as the Vancura Defence. } 1. { -KEY- } Rf8+ $1 { Transferring to f3 } Ke5 2. Rf3 $1 { We have completed the setup for the Vancura Defence. From here on, there are only four things to remember: 1. If you can give safely a check to the enemy King from the side, go for it. (An example of an unsafe side check is shown on move 8) 2. Otherwise, keep your Rook on the sixth rank to pressure the pawn from the side. 3. If the pawn ever moves to the seventh rank, play Ra3 and return to the drawing idea shown in Position 33. 4. If Black ever plays Ra2+, don't move your King to the promotion rank. } Ke4 3. Rb3 Kd4 4. Rf3 Kc4 5. Rf4+ Kc5 6. Rf5+ Kd6 7. Rf6+ Kd5 8. Rf3 $1 { Rf5 is not a safe check because the Black King will approach the White Rook, preventing Rf3 and any additional side checks. } ( 8. Rf5 $4 Ke4 9. Rf3 Rg1 10. Kf2 Rf1 11. Kxf1 Kxf3 ) 
